{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485516055,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTY0NDMxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1233#issuecomment-275644311"},"message":"Re your suspected \"reimagination\" of URLs: You probably mean the template replacement? This doesn't happen, since the passed URL isn't a template.\n\nBut the call to `AddSibling` with `recursive` probably is troublesome anyway, since we can pass things only wrt to the toplevel one. More complicated setups than the initally imagined ones will be tough that way, I think. If `CreateSibling` is redone without actual recursion, `AddSibling` should be called for each dataset separatly, I guess.\n\n\nRe RF proposal:\nWouldn't be necessary with an iterative approach as far as can see it ATM, since we then can pass all relevant information directly anyway. From my point of view you would \"centralize\" the core of `add-sibling` instead of the part, that could be reused with `create-sibling` and may be even `rewrite-urls`.\n\nBut in general: That comment is there for reason. So, I agree in not liking the current state. At that point I wanted to wait for us to know more cases for templates and \"real\" setups in order to figure out how to reasonably centralize it. \n\nConclusion: As of now, I'd prefer to just follow the same iterative approach as with other commands in `create-sibling`, calling `add-sibling` on a per-dataset basis (non-recursive) and leave the rest of it as is until we played with it a little bit more.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485546336,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDkzOTgwNjUxOQ=="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485699254,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTQwNTUyNDQ4"},"status":2}]}